1]defination= Python is an Open source, Free, High-level, Dynamic, and Interpreted programming language. Python was released in December 1989 by Guido van Rossum. Python programing language is one of the cleanest and easy to learn a language in the programming world. It’s easy syntax improved the readability of the code and makes it easy to understand.
2]Feactures of Python= 1. Easy to Learn and Read

Python has simple and clear syntax, so beginners can learn it quickly.
Its code looks almost like normal English, which makes it easy to understand.

2. Free and Open Source

Python is completely free to use.
Anyone can download it, use it, and even improve it because its source code is publicly available.

3. Object-Oriented Language

Python supports Object-Oriented Programming (OOP).
This helps programmers organize code using classes and objects, making large projects easier to manage.

4. Portable Language

Python programs can run on different operating systems like Windows, Linux, and Mac with very few changes.
This means the same code can work on many computers.

5. Large Library Support

Python provides many built-in libraries and tools.
These libraries help in web development, data science, AI, games, automation, and many other tasks without writing everything from scratch.

6. Interpreted Language

Python executes code line by line using an interpreter.
This makes debugging easier because errors can be found quickly during execution.

3]--------Advantages of Python-----------
Easy to learn
Simple and readable syntax
Less coding required
Large libraries available
Works on multiple platforms
Fast development
4]-------Disadvantages of Python---------
Slower execution speed
Uses more memory
Not ideal for mobile apps
Runtime errors possible
Weak for high-performance tasks
Less suitable for game development

5]  ------------Steps to Install Python on Windows-------------
Open the official website:
Python Downloads
Click Download Python.
Run the downloaded .exe file.
✔️ Tick “Add Python to PATH”.
Click Install Now.
Wait for installation to finish.
Click Close.
Verify installation:
Open Command Prompt

Type:

python --version
If version appears, Python is installed successfully.

6] The process to generate the output:
>> Write a high-level python code.
>> Save the code in py file.
>> Interprete the code.
>> It will generate a bytecode file.
>> The output will get printed on the screen.
